(Title) Tj
T*
(Efficacy and safety of a cosmetic anti-acne system versus prescription therapy in adults) Tj
T*
(with facial acne) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Background: Acne treatment options include prescription and non-prescription formulations) Tj
T*
(with varying tolerability profiles. We propose a comparative effectiveness trial of a) Tj
T*
(novel cosmetic anti-acne regimen versus established prescription therapy. Methods: Adults) Tj
T*
(aged 18-45 with mild-to-moderate facial acne \(n=54\) will be randomly assigned to either) Tj
T*
(cosmetic salicylic acid regimen \(1% cleanser plus 2% treatment lotion, twice daily\) or) Tj
T*
(prescription retinoid-benzoyl peroxide combination \(once daily\), applied to the entire) Tj
T*
(face for 12 weeks. Randomization will be stratified by skin type \(Fitzpatrick I-III versus) Tj
T*
(IV-VI\). Assessment timepoints: 48 hours, 4 weeks, 8 weeks, and 12 weeks. Primary outcome:) Tj
T*
(clinician-assessed acne severity score. Secondary outcomes: total lesion count, post-) Tj
T*
(inflammatory hyperpigmentation/erythema, sebum production, and skin irritation scores.) Tj
T*
(Tolerability will be measured via validated scales for dryness, redness, and stinging) Tj
T*
(sensations. Inclusion: active facial acne without recent systemic acne medications.) Tj
T*
(Blinding: investigator and participant blinded to treatment allocation. Study design:) Tj
T*
(single-center, double-blind, randomized, active-controlled trial.) Tj
ET
